    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0173" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/418</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-02T20:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 8, 11 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1462. Yesterday’s demonstration against Provisional Government disappointing to
                    projectors. Cossacks and loyal soldiers at 3 this morning arrested 68 anarchists
                    who had undisputed possession of Durnovo Palace two months and who last evening
                    compelled prison keeper to release several criminals. This by order of
                    Provisional Government. Enthusiastic impromptu demonstration now being held
                    incited by decisive victory for Russian forces on southeast front, 9,000
                    prisoners taken. Outlook for Government more encouraging than for weeks
                    past.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
